OFFICTAL USE ONLY
Tarqul Frumos. May 1944A German Panzer Division under General Hasso von Manteuffeland a soviet tank army (or motorized army) opposed each other ona broad open plain in the Battle of Targul Frumos. Speed andmaneuverability were the important factors and in these the GermanMark IVs and Mark VIs surpassed the powerfully gunned Soviet JS-III.The Russians were able to surprise the Germans by opening fire withtheir high-velocity 120mm. gun at a range whieh was far beyond theeffective range of the German tank guns. when the Germans werewlthin their normal firing range their guns were unable to penetratethe heavy soviet armor. The Germans closed the distance quicklyand, due to superion mobility, maneuvered around the Russian tanksto hit their thinner side and rear armor. The result was a cl_ear-cut Getrnan victory, achieved by superior leadership and tacticarability and faciritated by certain weaknesses in the JS-rrr--aslow hand traverse mechanism for a very heavy turret, a meagersupply of ammunition because the rounds were so lange that fewerrounds firred up more space, and heavy separate hand-loading am-munition that srowed the rate of fire. of a totar of 4I0 tanksthe Russians lost 350 and 60 others were damaged; the Germansl-ost only 11 tanks out of a total of 160.
