OFFICIAL USE ONLY
III. ANALYSISA study of the arrnored force engagements contained in thisstudy suggest that there are three major kinds of tank operationalcharacteristics, and two important subsidiary characteristics,which affect the outcome of armored engagements. These fivechanacteristics, listed in what appears to be the order of theirrelative importance, are as follows:1. Tactical Mobilitv (substantial speed combined with cross-country capability under any likeIy combat circurnstances, to in-clude if possible a sright margin of superiority over enemy tanksof comparable role and characteristics. )2. Firepowel (Ability to fire quickly, accuratery, and re-peatedry, with a weapon whose pnojectile has sufficient mass andmuzzle velocity to destroy a likely opposing tank at reasonablerange. )
3. Protection (Fu11
protection against smalI arns, shell
fragments, and long-range fire fnom the most likely possiblearmored opponent. )4. Endurancs (Ability to operate effectively oven substan-tial per.iods of time and extensive distances; this is also an as-pect of strategic mobility, and is enhanced by well-organizedlogistical support. )
