That such data can be found seems certain, but even that for USfonces is not readily available in this country, and in some in-stances it would be necessary to obtain access to German (and pos-sibly Brltish) archival materials.As a result, we have not been able to give sufficient con-sideratj.on to the openational characteristics of endurance andreliability, nor to the effects of sustained operations on leader-ship and on troops in their penformance in anmored conflict.
Svstematic Approach to Remove LimitationsF'our specific actions could be taken to develop a researchplan which would both profit from what has been accomplished inthis study, and would at the same time assure the comprehensive-ness and catholcity which was not possible in this study in thetime available:1. Review each of the engagements examined in detail inthis study to ascertain which ones could profit from expansion,and the availability of more data, and which ones could be re-lated either to subsequent or to prior operations, in order toprovide greater insights into the operational tank characteristicsof endurance and reliability.2, Ascertain what information is needed, and where it islikely to be available, for impontant anmored conflict and opera-tions experience in mode::n history which has not been cove::ed
