OFFTCIAL USE ONLY
It is evident, then, that further extensive research in atlthese reconds can perform two impcrtant kinds of functions. First,the records can be exploited system a tically to provide the kindsof information needed to assist in important poricy decisions oncurrent military problems of procurement, desigar, or tactics, asin the case of this study. Second, these records can provide abasj.s for equally systematic verification on validation of theresults of wargames.There are a nurnber of ways in which these records could besystematically mined and the results analyzed to accomplish theseobjectives. One possibility would be to establish an i.nstitutefor military operational records evaluation, which might operatemuch as the Navyrs George Washington University Logistics ResearchProject operates. This and othen possibilities should be exploredfor the benefit of aII of the military services, of the Departmentof Defense, and in particular the Office of the Assistant Secre-tary of Defense (Systems Analysis). Such an institute, further:-more, could provide bases for modified combat reporting systems,to remedy in the future reporting deficiencies of the past.
